    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\nHere's what I changed to satisfy the specification:\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (the create-owner logic):\n- **Deterministic `householdId`**: the `householdId(...)` helper now returns the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)` (new `sha256Hex12` helper) instead of a UUID over last-name+address. Every owner now gets a `householdId` regardless of creation order or membership, so owners sharing last name + postcode share it automatically.\n- **`sharesHousehold` only bypasses the block**: removed the old backfill code that \"created the link.\" The household link is now purely derived. A second owner in an existing household (same computed `householdId`) is rejected with **409 `DuplicateHouseholdException`** unless the request sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member.\n- **Everything keys off the computed `householdId`**: household-member detection (which feeds `householdSize`) and the identity-key duplicate check both recompute the household id from `(lastName, postcode)` rather than relying on the old address-based/stored value.\n- **Declared members aren't flagged**: `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` are cleared \u2014 a same-household owner is either rejected (409) or, when declared, created without a suspected-duplicate flag. Removed the now-dead soft-duplicate scan and unused `Comparator`/`UUID` imports.\n\n**Supporting docs/handlers** (kept faithful to the new keying):\n- `ExceptionControllerAdvice` now reports the household conflict on `lastName`/`postcode` (was `lastName`/`address`).\n- Updated `DuplicateHouseholdException` javadoc and the `sharesHousehold`/`householdId` descriptions in `openapi.yml`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` passes: same last name + postcode yield the same `householdId` (with `sharesHousehold` bypassing the 409), and a different last name yields a different one.",
